<article class="env-definition" id="0E2C">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0E2C">Definition <span data-tag="0E2C">47.27.1</span>.</a> Let $R \to A$ be a flat ring map of finite presentation. A <em>relative dualizing complex</em> is an object $K \in D(A)$ such that </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$K$ is $R$-perfect (More on Algebra, Definition <a href="/tag/0DHS" data-tag="0DHS">15.85.1</a>), and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$R\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{A \otimes _ R A}(A, K \otimes _ A^\mathbf {L} (A \otimes _ R A))$ is isomorphic to $A$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>